dsh-progress-history
====================

This package is an independent DSH plugin (MIT). It does not contain code from
other packages; it reads a session record format produced by a separate
third-party plugin.

Data source it consumes
-----------------------
- Plugin:  dsh-progress-summary  (MIT, https://github.com/tastynoob/dsh-progress-summary)
- Record:  plugin:progress-summary/line  (an "ignorable" session plugin record)
- Fields:  { line: string, state: string, turn: number, at: number, calls: number }

That record type is owned by dsh-progress-summary. This package only reads it
through DSH's public plugin-record and session-projection APIs
(`@deepseek-ai/dsh-session`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection`). If the
upstream plugin is not installed, this panel renders an explanatory empty state.

DSH itself (DeepSeek Harness) is a separate MIT-licensed product; this package
uses only its documented extension points (bundle patch, client module loader,
slots, sidebarRightTabs).
